@using Backlog.Modules.Sessions.Abstractions
@using Backlog.UI.Components.Integrations
@inject IServiceProvider Services
@implements IDisposable

@*
    The pull requests pane: the open pull requests of every registered repository,
    triaged. Four lane tiles say how many need the reader, are ready to merge, wait
    on somebody else, or are still drafts; the list below is grouped by those lanes;
    and the pull request the reader picked is laid out beside it — one verdict on what
    stands between it and its merge, with the act that fits, then the four things
    GitHub gates a merge on, its checks one by one, its stack, and the task and the
    session it came from.

    A verdict rather than a row of badges, because a reader acts on one thing at a
    time (.devbook/domain/sessions/features.md#one-verdict-per-pull-request). It is
    PullRequestVerdict's to derive; this pane only draws it, and its acts are the
    only ones the banner offers — plus Cancel auto-merge wherever GitHub already
    holds an auto-merge the verdict's acts do not withdraw, because that undoes a
    request rather than making one.

    It is the Sessions context's second surface, what the sessions shipped, and it
    lives in the shell project rather than beside SessionsPane for one reason: it
    reads GitHub through the GitHub adapter, and ModuleBoundaryTests holds every
    Sessions project to referencing no infrastructure at all. The shell already
    takes that adapter for Settings and the Tasks merge menu, so the screen sits
    where the reference is allowed rather than the rule bending to where the screen
    would otherwise sit.

    Like the sessions pane it owns its own loading and is not a monitor: it reads
    GitHub when it opens, when somebody presses Refresh, and — for one repository —
    after an act, and never on a timer. A list that re-read itself would spend a
    GraphQL query per repository every few seconds to tell a reader what they could
    have asked for.

    It has two views. Open is the one it opens on, with the lanes and the acts.
    Recently merged is what the open list cannot show — a pull request merged from it
    leaves it — and is read on the first switch to it rather than on open, because
    most opens never look at it; once read it is kept until Refresh, an act, or the
    next open. A merged pull request is in no lane, so that view has no tiles.

    Every repository is read, and the header's chips narrow what is drawn, the way
    the session list narrows its rows. Reading only the scoped ones would make every
    press on a chip a round trip to GitHub, and the chips are pressed far more often
    than the list goes stale.

    What the detail links to is the shell's to answer. A task is an entry, which
    belongs to Tasks; this pane asks for the reference by repository and number and
    hands it back on a click. A session is matched here, because the sessions are
    this context's own: first the session whose transcript recorded the pull
    request's address, then the most recent session that ran on its head branch in
    the same repository — the second is how a Copilot session, which records no pull
    request, still leads back to the work.

    The ✕ only reports that it was pressed; what that closes is the shell's business.

    Four things narrow the rows beside the header's chips: Mine (the reader's own
    pull requests and those related to one of their tasks), a repository's label
    filter, set in Settings, which lets through only pull requests carrying one of its
    labels, and the lane a tile was pressed for. A pinned pull request ignores all of
    them: a pin is somebody saying "keep this one in front of me". It is read by
    number beside the open list, so it stays — merged or closed, with no act and no
    place in a stack — until it is unpinned, and it sits in a Pinned group of its own
    at the top.
*@

<section @key=@("pull-requests-pane") class="pull-requests-panel" id="pull-requests-pane" aria-labelledby="pull-requests-title" data-testid="pull-requests-panel">
    <SectionHeader BaseClass="pull-requests-panel__header"
                   TextCssClass=""
                   EyebrowCssClass="pull-requests-panel__eyebrow"
                   TitleCssClass="pull-requests-panel__title"
                   DescriptionCssClass="pull-requests-panel__subtitle"
                   DescriptionTestId="pull-requests-subtitle"
                   ActionsCssClass="pull-requests-panel__header-actions"
                   Eyebrow="Pull requests"
                   TitleId="pull-requests-title"
                   Title="@(Merged ? "Recently merged on GitHub" : "Open on GitHub")"
                   Description="@Subtitle">
        <Actions>
            @if (Configured)
            {
                <Badge BaseClass="pull-requests-panel__count" Kind="" TestId="pull-requests-count">@CountLabel</Badge>
            }
            <IconButton AriaLabel="Close pull requests pane" CssClass="btn--ghost" OnClick="() => OnClose.InvokeAsync()">✕</IconButton>
        </Actions>
    </SectionHeader>

    @if (!Configured)
    {
        @* Nothing to read until a repository is registered, and the sentence says
           where that is done rather than drawing an empty list that suggests the
           repositories have no pull requests. *@
        <EmptyState Title="No repositories registered"
                    Description="Register a GitHub repository in Settings, and its open pull requests are listed here."
                    TestId="pull-requests-not-configured" />
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="pull-requests-panel__filters" data-testid="pull-requests-filters">
            @* Which list, as a strip beside whose: the two are independent questions,
               and Mine means the same thing in both views. Back to Open on every
               open, for the reason Mine comes back. *@
            <div class="pull-requests-filter">
                <span class="pull-requests-filter__label">View</span>
                <ButtonGroup AriaLabel="Which pull requests to list" TestId="pull-requests-view">
                    <ToggleButton Pressed="!Merged"
                                  PressedChanged="_ => ShowAsync(PullRequestsView.Open)"
                                  TestId="pull-requests-view-open">
                        Open
                    </ToggleButton>
                    <ToggleButton Pressed="Merged"
                                  PressedChanged="_ => ShowAsync(PullRequestsView.RecentlyMerged)"
                                  TestId="pull-requests-view-merged">
                        Recently merged
                    </ToggleButton>
                </ButtonGroup>
            </div>

            @* A one-of-many strip, like the session list's Show, and for its reason:
               it comes back to Mine on every open, and a switch that forgot its
               setting would read as broken where a strip that returns to its first
               option reads as where you are looking. *@
            <div class="pull-requests-filter">
                <span class="pull-requests-filter__label">Show</span>
                <ButtonGroup AriaLabel="Whose pull requests to show" TestId="pull-requests-author-filter">
                    <ToggleButton Pressed="_mine"
                                  PressedChanged="_ => _mine = true"
                                  TestId="pull-requests-filter-mine">
                        Mine
                    </ToggleButton>
                    <ToggleButton Pressed="!_mine"
                                  PressedChanged="_ => _mine = false"
                                  TestId="pull-requests-filter-everyone">
                        Everyone's
                    </ToggleButton>
                </ButtonGroup>
            </div>

            <div class="pull-requests-filter pull-requests-filter--end">
                <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Secondary"
                           Disabled="@Loading"
                           TestId="pull-requests-refresh"
                           OnClick="RefreshViewAsync">
                    @(Loading ? "Reading..." : "Refresh")
                </AppButton>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pull-requests-panel__content" id="pull-requests-content" aria-busy="@(Loading ? "true" : null)">
            @if (_notice is not null)
            {
                @* Only where the host composed no toast channel: an act's outcome has
                   to reach the reader somewhere, and this is the pane's own line for
                   it. *@
                <Alert Message="@_notice" BaseClass="pull-requests-panel__notice" Role="status" TestId="pull-requests-outcome" />
            }
            @if (Failures.Count > 0)
            {
                @* Named per repository, and a failure rather than news: that
                   repository's read did not complete. The rows below are every
                   other repository's, complete, which the sentence says so a reader
                   does not wonder whether the whole list is suspect. *@
                <Alert Message="@FailureMessage"
                       BaseClass="pull-requests-panel__notice"
                       Role="alert"
                       ActionLabel="Retry"
                       OnAction="RefreshViewAsync"
                       ActionTestId="pull-requests-unreadable-retry"
                       TestId="pull-requests-unreadable" />
            }
            @if (Merged && _merged is { Truncated.Count: > 0 } truncated)
            {
                @* Not a failure — every row below is real — but the window is not
                   complete for these, and the subtitle promises fourteen days. *@
                <Alert Message="@TruncatedMessage(truncated.Truncated)"
                       BaseClass="pull-requests-panel__notice"
                       Role="status"
                       TestId="pull-requests-merged-truncated" />
            }
            @if (_sessionsUnreadable)
            {
                <Alert Message="Couldn't read the session records on this PC, so no pull request is matched to a session."
                       BaseClass="pull-requests-panel__notice"
                       Role="status"
                       TestId="pull-requests-sessions-unreadable" />
            }

            @if (Loading && !ViewRead)
            {
                <div class="pull-requests-panel__loading" data-testid="pull-requests-loading" aria-hidden="true">
                    @foreach (var width in SkeletonWidths)
                    {
                        <Skeleton Shape="SkeletonShape.Block" Width="@width" />
                    }
                </div>
            }
            else
            {
                var board = Merged ? MergedBoard() : OpenBoard();

                @if (!Merged)
                {
                    @* One lane at a time, pressed again to let go: a filter by what a
                       pull request needs, counted over what Mine, the scope and the
                       label filters leave. Each tile says why in a line, so a count
                       is never the only thing it carries. *@
                    <div class="pull-requests-lanes" role="group" aria-label="Filter by what a pull request needs" data-testid="pull-requests-lanes">
                        @foreach (var tile in board.Lanes)
                        {
                            var lane = tile.Lane;
                            <ToggleButton BaseClass="@($"pull-requests-lane pull-requests-lane--{LaneTone(lane)}")"
                                          PressedCssClass="pull-requests-lane--pressed"
                                          Pressed="@(_lane == lane)"
                                          PressedChanged="_ => PressLane(lane)"
                                          TestId="@($"pull-requests-lane-{LaneSlug(lane)}")"
                                          data-lane="@LaneSlug(lane)">
                                <span class="pull-requests-lane__label"><span class="pull-requests-lane__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>@LaneLabel(lane)</span>
                                <span class="pull-requests-lane__number">@tile.Total</span>
                                <span class="pull-requests-lane__reasons">@tile.Reasons</span>
                            </ToggleButton>
                        }
                    </div>
                }

                <div class="pull-requests-board">
                    <section class="pull-requests-list" aria-label="@(Merged ? "Pull requests merged recently" : "Open pull requests")">
                        @if (board.Groups.Count == 0)
                        {
                            <EmptyState Title="@ListEmptyTitle" Description="@ListEmptyDescription" TestId="pull-requests-empty" />
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            @foreach (var group in board.Groups)
                            {
                                <section @key="group.Slug" class="pull-requests-group" data-testid="pull-requests-group" data-lane="@group.Slug" aria-label="@group.Label">
                                    <h3 class="pull-requests-group__heading">@group.Label <span class="pull-requests-group__size">@group.Rows.Count</span></h3>
                                    <div class="pull-requests-group__rows">
                                        @foreach (var row in group.Rows)
                                        {
                                            var key = row.Key;
                                            <ToggleButton @key="key"
                                                          BaseClass="@RowClass(row)"
                                                          PressedCssClass="pull-requests-row--selected"
                                                          Pressed="@(board.Selected?.Key == key)"
                                                          PressedChanged="_ => _selected = key"
                                                          TestId="pull-request-row"
                                                          @attributes="RowAttributes(row)">
                                                @RowBody(row)
                                            </ToggleButton>
                                        }
                                    </div>
                                </section>
                            }
                        }
                    </section>

                    @if (board.Selected is { } selected)
                    {
                        @Detail(selected)
                    }
                </div>
            }
        </div>
    }
</section>

@code {
    /// <summary>The two lists the pane can show.</summary>
    private enum PullRequestsView
    {
        Open,
        RecentlyMerged
    }

    /// <summary>How many of a pull request's checks the detail lists before it counts
    /// the rest: enough for every failure a typical run has, few enough that the stack
    /// and the cards below are still on screen.</summary>
    private const int ChecksShown = 6;

    private static readonly string[] SkeletonWidths = ["100%", "92%", "96%", "88%"];

    /// <summary>The lanes in the order the tiles and the groups are drawn: the one that
    /// needs the reader first.</summary>
    private static readonly PullRequestLane[] Lanes = Enum.GetValues<PullRequestLane>();

    private GitHubIntegration? _gitHub;
    private IAgentSessionSource? _sessionSource;
    private IToastChannel? _toasts;
    private PullRequestPinsStore? _pins;
    private TimeProvider _clock = TimeProvider.System;

    private GitHubPullRequestListing _listing = GitHubPullRequestListing.Empty;

    /// <summary>The pinned pull requests, read by number whatever state they are in.
    /// Only the ones still pinned and not in <see cref="_listing"/> are drawn from
    /// here: for an open one the open list's row is the same pull request.</summary>
    private GitHubPullRequestListing _pinned = GitHubPullRequestListing.Empty;

    /// <summary>Bumped on every pin and unpin, so what is derived from the pins is
    /// derived again.</summary>
    private int _pinsVersion;
    private IReadOnlyList<AgentSession> _sessions = [];
    private bool _sessionsUnreadable;

    /// <summary>Reads in flight. A count rather than a flag, because switching views
    /// while the open list is still being read starts the merged read beside it, and
    /// the first to finish must not say the second has.</summary>
    private int _reads;

    private bool Loading => _reads > 0;

    private bool Merged => _view is PullRequestsView.RecentlyMerged;

    /// <summary>Whether the view in front of the reader has been read once, so the
    /// placeholder rows are a first read's and never a refresh's.</summary>
    private bool ViewRead => Merged ? _merged is not null : _read;

    /// <summary>Whether the list has been read once, so the placeholder rows are a
    /// first read's and never a refresh's.</summary>
    private bool _read;

    /// <summary>Open on every open, for the reason <see cref="_mine"/> is Mine.</summary>
    private PullRequestsView _view = PullRequestsView.Open;

    /// <summary>The merged view's read, or null until the first switch to it — and
    /// again after Refresh on the open view or an act, either of which can have
    /// changed what was merged, so the next switch reads it afresh.</summary>
    private GitHubMergedPullRequestListing? _merged;

    /// <summary>Which merged read may still land. Bumped by every new read and by every
    /// invalidation, so a read that an act or a newer read overtook while it was out
    /// cannot write its older answer back over the newer one.</summary>
    private int _mergedGeneration;

    /// <summary>The merged read in flight, so switching away and back while it is out
    /// waits on it rather than sending a second.</summary>
    private Task? _mergedRead;

    /// <summary>When the merged view was read, so "2h ago" is measured against the
    /// reading and a re-render does not move it.</summary>
    private DateTimeOffset _mergedReadAt;

    /// <summary>Mine by default and on every open: the list a person opens this for
    /// is their own, and a stored choice would open it on everybody's without their
    /// having asked.</summary>
    private bool _mine = true;

    /// <summary>The lane a tile was pressed for, or null for every lane. Null on every
    /// open, and let go on the switch to Recently merged, where no pull request is in
    /// a lane.</summary>
    private PullRequestLane? _lane;

    /// <summary>The pull request the reader picked, by <see cref="Key"/>; null for
    /// the first one listed. Kept while a filter hides it — the detail falls back to
    /// the first row shown — so letting the filter go brings the pick back.</summary>
    private string? _selected;

    /// <summary>The rows an act is running on, by <see cref="Key"/>. Their actions
    /// are disabled until the re-read after the act has landed, because a second act
    /// started in between would act on a row the first has just made stale.</summary>
    private readonly HashSet<string> _busy = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    /// <summary>An act's outcome, where the host composed no toast channel.</summary>
    private string? _notice;

    /// <summary>Raised when somebody dismisses the pane; what that closes is the
    /// shell's decision.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnClose { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The repositories the shell has scoped, by alias, in the order taken;
    /// empty for all of them. Read on every render, as the session list reads it.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<string> RepositoryScope { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>What a repository is called here — the configured alias for an
    /// <c>owner/name</c> — or null for one this workspace does not know. The shell's
    /// to answer, as it is for the session list; without it the pane asks the
    /// adapter's own registry, which is the same list.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Func<string?, string?>? RepositoryAlias { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Which identity hue a repository wears, or null. The shell's, for the
    /// reason <c>SessionsPane.RepositoryColour</c> is.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Func<string?, int?>? RepositoryColour { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// The Backlog entry a pull request belongs to, or null. With the flag set, only
    /// among the reader's own tasks — what Mine adds to the pull requests they opened.
    /// Asked of the shell because the relations are on the entries, and entries
    /// belong to Tasks.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Func<PullRequestTaskSubject, bool, DeliveryRunReference?>? PullRequestTask { get; set; }

    /// <summary>How the shell opens that entry. Without it the task renders as inert
    /// text rather than as a control that would have to refuse the click.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<DeliveryRunReference> OnOpenTask { get; set; }

    /// <summary>How the shell opens the session list on one session, by its id.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnOpenSession { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether there is anything to read: the adapter composed, and at least
    /// one repository registered with it.</summary>
    private bool Configured => _gitHub is { IsConfigured: true };

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Each one optional, the way the session list resolves its record keeper: a
        // host without GitHub is the not-configured state, a host without sessions
        // simply links no session, and a host without toasts gets the inline line.
        _gitHub = Services.GetService<GitHubIntegration>();
        _sessionSource = Services.GetService<IAgentSessionSource>();
        _toasts = Services.GetService<IToastChannel>();
        _pins = Services.GetService<PullRequestPinsStore>();
        _clock = Services.GetService<TimeProvider>() ?? TimeProvider.System;

        // A pin or a label filter changed — here or in Settings — redraws the rows
        // from what was read; only a pin nothing read yet costs a read.
        if (_pins is not null) _pins.Changed += OnPinsChanged;
        if (_gitHub is not null) _gitHub.Settings.Changed += OnSettingsChanged;

        await ReadOpenAsync();
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        if (_pins is not null) _pins.Changed -= OnPinsChanged;
        if (_gitHub is not null) _gitHub.Settings.Changed -= OnSettingsChanged;
    }

    private void OnSettingsChanged() => _ = InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);

    private void OnPinsChanged() => _ = InvokeAsync(async () =>
    {
        _pinsVersion++;
        StateHasChanged();

        if (PinsUnread())
        {
            await ReadPinnedAndRenderAsync();
        }
    });

    private async Task ReadPinnedAndRenderAsync()
    {
        _reads++;
        try
        {
            await ReadPinnedAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _reads--;
        }

        StateHasChanged();
    }

    /// <summary>Whether a pin names a pull request neither read has brought in — one
    /// pinned from the merged view, or on another window.</summary>
    private bool PinsUnread()
    {
        if (_pins is null) return false;

        var read = _listing.PullRequests.Concat(_pinned.PullRequests).Select(Key).ToHashSet(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        return _pins.Pins.Any(pin => !read.Contains(Key(pin.RepositoryFullName, pin.Number)));
    }

    /// <summary>Which pinned read may still land. Bumped by every pinned read, so two
    /// out at once — a pin made while another pin's read is out, or beside the open
    /// read — cannot land in network order and leave the older answer, which lacks
    /// the newer pin, as the last word.</summary>
    private int _pinnedGeneration;

    /// <summary>One pinned read, kept only if no newer one started while it was out.</summary>
    private async Task ReadPinnedAsync()
    {
        var generation = ++_pinnedGeneration;
        var listing = await ReadPinsAsync();

        if (generation == _pinnedGeneration) _pinned = listing;
    }

    /// <summary>Every pin, read by number. No pins, no request.</summary>
    private async Task<GitHubPullRequestListing> ReadPinsAsync()
    {
        if (_gitHub is not { } gitHub || _pins is not { Pins.Count: > 0 } pins) return GitHubPullRequestListing.Empty;

        return await gitHub.ListPinnedPullRequestsAsync(pins.Pins);
    }

    private bool IsPinned(string repositoryFullName, int number) => _pins?.IsPinned(repositoryFullName, number) == true;

    private bool IsPinned(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) => IsPinned(pull.RepositoryFullName, pull.Number);

    /// <summary>Pins or unpins one pull request. The store announces it, and
    /// <see cref="OnPinsChanged"/> does the rest.</summary>
    private void TogglePin(string repositoryFullName, int number)
    {
        if (_pins is null) return;

        if (_pins.IsPinned(repositoryFullName, number)) _pins.Unpin(repositoryFullName, number);
        else _pins.Pin(repositoryFullName, number);
    }

    /// <summary>Shows a view, reading the merged one the first time it is shown. The
    /// merged view has no lanes, so the lane is let go on the way there rather than
    /// waiting, invisible, to narrow the open view on the way back.</summary>
    private async Task ShowAsync(PullRequestsView view)
    {
        _view = view;

        if (view is PullRequestsView.RecentlyMerged)
        {
            _lane = null;
            await EnsureMergedAsync();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>A tile pressed: its lane, or every lane again when it already was.</summary>
    private void PressLane(PullRequestLane lane) => _lane = _lane == lane ? null : lane;

    /// <summary>The merged view's read: none when it is already in, the one in flight
    /// when there is one, else a new one.</summary>
    private Task EnsureMergedAsync()
    {
        if (_merged is not null) return Task.CompletedTask;
        if (_mergedRead is { IsCompleted: false } inFlight) return inFlight;

        return _mergedRead = ReadMergedAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>Drops the merged view's copy and any read still out for it: something
    /// has happened since that either may not know about.</summary>
    private void InvalidateMerged()
    {
        _merged = null;
        _mergedRead = null;
        _mergedGeneration++;
    }

    /// <summary>Refresh and Retry: the view in front of the reader, read again. A
    /// fresh look at the open list also drops the merged view's copy, which is older
    /// than it now and is read again when next shown.</summary>
    private Task RefreshViewAsync()
    {
        if (Merged) return _mergedRead = ReadMergedAsync();

        InvalidateMerged();
        return ReadOpenAsync();
    }

    private async Task ReadOpenAsync()
    {
        if (_gitHub is not { IsConfigured: true } gitHub) return;

        _reads++;

        try
        {
            // Both in flight together: GitHub and the session folders are two
            // readers that need nothing from each other until both are in.
            var listing = gitHub.ListOpenPullRequestsAsync(gitHub.Repositories);
            var pinned = ReadPinnedAsync();
            var sessions = ReadSessionsAsync();

            _listing = await listing;
            await pinned;
            _sessions = await sessions;
            _read = true;
        }
        finally
        {
            _reads--;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>One merged read. Its answer is kept only if nothing superseded it while
    /// it was out — a newer read, or an act or open-list refresh that invalidated it.</summary>
    private async Task ReadMergedAsync()
    {
        if (_gitHub is not { IsConfigured: true } gitHub) return;

        var generation = ++_mergedGeneration;
        _reads++;

        try
        {
            var merged = gitHub.ListMergedPullRequestsAsync(gitHub.Repositories);
            var sessions = ReadSessionsAsync();

            var listing = await merged;
            var read = await sessions;

            if (generation != _mergedGeneration) return;

            _merged = listing;
            _mergedReadAt = _clock.GetUtcNow();
            _sessions = read;
        }
        finally
        {
            _reads--;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The sessions to match rows against, or none when there is no source.
    /// A source that cannot be read is said out loud and costs the session card
    /// only: the pull requests are GitHub's and do not depend on it.</summary>
    private async Task<IReadOnlyList<AgentSession>> ReadSessionsAsync()
    {
        _sessionsUnreadable = false;

        if (_sessionSource is null) return [];

        try
        {
            return (await _sessionSource.GetSessionsAsync()).Sessions;
        }
        catch (Exception exception) when (exception is IOException or UnauthorizedAccessException)
        {
            _sessionsUnreadable = true;
            return [];
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Reads one repository again and puts its rows in place of the old ones. After
    /// an act, because only that repository can have moved because of it — and a
    /// merged pull request leaves the list here, which is the act's own answer.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task RereadAsync(string repositoryFullName)
    {
        if (_gitHub is not { } gitHub) return;

        var repository = gitHub.Repositories.FirstOrDefault(candidate =>
                string.Equals(candidate.FullName, repositoryFullName, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
            ?? RepositoryOf(gitHub, repositoryFullName);

        if (repository is null) return;

        // A pin in this repository is read again beside it: a pinned pull request the
        // act merged leaves the open list, and only the pinned read says it merged.
        var hasPins = _pins?.Pins.Any(pin => string.Equals(pin.RepositoryFullName, repositoryFullName, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)) == true;
        var rereadPins = hasPins ? ReadPinnedAsync() : null;

        var reread = await gitHub.ListOpenPullRequestsAsync([repository]);
        if (rereadPins is not null) await rereadPins;

        bool Other(string fullName) => !string.Equals(fullName, repositoryFullName, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

        _listing = new GitHubPullRequestListing(
            [.. _listing.PullRequests.Where(pull => Other(pull.RepositoryFullName))
                .Concat(reread.PullRequests)
                .OrderByDescending(pull => pull.UpdatedAt)],
            [.. _listing.Failures.Where(failure => Other(failure.RepositoryFullName)).Concat(reread.Failures)]);
    }

    private static GitHubRepositoryRef? RepositoryOf(GitHubIntegration gitHub, string fullName)
    {
        var parts = fullName.Split('/', 2);
        return parts.Length == 2 ? gitHub.RepositoryFor(parts[0], parts[1]) : null;
    }

    private Task UpdateBranchAsync(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) =>
        ActAsync(pull, gitHub => gitHub.UpdateBranchAsync(pull), $"Asked GitHub to update the branch of {Subject(pull)}.");

    private Task RerunFailedAsync(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) =>
        ActAsync(pull, gitHub => gitHub.RerunFailedChecksAsync(pull), $"Asked GitHub to re-run the failed checks of {Subject(pull)}.");

    private Task MarkReadyAsync(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) =>
        ActAsync(pull, gitHub => gitHub.MarkReadyForReviewAsync(pull), $"{Subject(pull)} is ready for review.");

    /// <summary>The merge act, re-derived at the click from the row as it stands —
    /// the same answer as when the button was drawn unless a read landed in between,
    /// and then the newer one is the one to act on.</summary>
    private Task MergeAsync(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) => OfferedMergeFor(pull) switch
    {
        PullRequestMerge.Now => ActAsync(pull, gitHub => gitHub.MergePullRequestAsync(pull.ToStatus()), $"Merged {Subject(pull)}."),
        PullRequestMerge.WhenChecksPass => ActAsync(pull, gitHub => gitHub.EnableAutoMergeAsync(pull.ToStatus()), $"{Subject(pull)} will merge when it is ready."),
        PullRequestMerge.CancelAutoMerge => ActAsync(pull, gitHub => gitHub.DisableAutoMergeAsync(pull.ToStatus()), $"Cancelled auto-merge for {Subject(pull)}."),
        _ => Task.CompletedTask
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// One act, and the read that follows it whether it worked or not. After a
    /// success the read is what shows the result; after a refusal it is what corrects
    /// a row that had moved on since it was drawn. The refusal itself arrives already
    /// worded by the adapter, naming the act and the pull request.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ActAsync(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull, Func<GitHubIntegration, Task> act, string done)
    {
        if (_gitHub is not { } gitHub || !_busy.Add(Key(pull))) return;

        try
        {
            try
            {
                await act(gitHub);
                Publish(ToastMessage.Info(done, "pull-requests-act-done"));
            }
            catch (Exception exception) when (exception is GitHubException or GitHubNotConfiguredException or HttpRequestException)
            {
                Publish(ToastMessage.Error(exception.Message, "pull-requests-act-failed"));
            }

            // A merge — now, or by auto-merge while the reader looks elsewhere — is
            // something the merged view's copy cannot know about.
            InvalidateMerged();

            await RereadAsync(pull.RepositoryFullName);

            // The reader may have switched to the merged view while the act was out;
            // the read it started was just superseded, so it is sent again.
            if (Merged) await EnsureMergedAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _busy.Remove(Key(pull));
        }
    }

    private void Publish(ToastMessage message)
    {
        if (_toasts is not null)
        {
            _toasts.Publish(message);
            return;
        }

        _notice = message.Message;
    }

    private bool Busy(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) => _busy.Contains(Key(pull));

    private static string Key(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) => Key(pull.RepositoryFullName, pull.Number);

    private static string Key(string repositoryFullName, int number) => $"{repositoryFullName}#{number}";

    private static string Subject(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) => $"{pull.RepositoryFullName}#{pull.Number}";

    /// <summary>What the merge button does for this pull request, or null for none.
    /// Queued already comes first, for the reason the task row's merge menu gives:
    /// enabling again would be refused, and merging now would jump the queue it was
    /// put in on purpose. A draft is offered nothing else — GitHub merges no draft, and
    /// "Ready for review" is the act it is waiting on. Nor is a branch in conflict:
    /// "when checks pass" would wait on checks that may already pass while the
    /// conflict, which only a change to the branch resolves, is what holds it — the
    /// verdict says so instead.</summary>
    internal static PullRequestMerge? MergeActFor(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) =>
        pull.AutoMergeEnabled ? PullRequestMerge.CancelAutoMerge
        : pull.IsDraft || pull.HasConflicts ? null
        : pull.MergeReady ? PullRequestMerge.Now
        : PullRequestMerge.WhenChecksPass;

    /// <summary>The merge act this pull request offers: <see cref="MergeActFor"/>, less
    /// a merge on a pull request that waits on another in its stack — merged now, it
    /// would land on its parent's branch rather than where the stack is going, and
    /// "Waits on" says so instead. Withdrawing auto-merge stays, because that undoes a
    /// request rather than making one.</summary>
    private PullRequestMerge? OfferedMergeFor(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) =>
        pull.IsOpen
        && MergeActFor(pull) is { } act
        && (act is PullRequestMerge.CancelAutoMerge || Stacks.ParentOf(pull) is null)
            ? act
            : null;

    /// <summary>The merge button's words. Handing it to auto-merge reads "Merge when
    /// ready", the verdict table's word in <c>features.md#one-verdict-per-pull-request</c>:
    /// GitHub merges it once everything it waits on is through — checks, a required
    /// review, or both — so naming only the checks would send a reader whose pull
    /// request waits for an approval to look at the wrong thing.</summary>
    private static string MergeLabel(PullRequestMerge act) => act switch
    {
        PullRequestMerge.Now => "Merge now",
        PullRequestMerge.CancelAutoMerge => "Cancel auto-merge",
        PullRequestMerge.WhenChecksPass => "Merge when ready"
    };

    // --- What is read, narrowed ------------------------------------------------

    private bool Scoped => RepositoryScope.Count > 0;

    private string ScopeLabel => string.Join(", ", RepositoryScope);

    /// <summary>The alias a repository goes by here: the shell's answer, else the
    /// adapter's registry, else nothing.</summary>
    private string? AliasOf(string? repository)
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(repository)) return null;

        return RepositoryAlias?.Invoke(repository)
            ?? _gitHub?.Repositories.FirstOrDefault(candidate =>
                string.Equals(candidate.FullName, repository, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                || string.Equals(candidate.Alias, repository, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))?.Alias;
    }

    private bool InScope(string repositoryFullName) =>
        !Scoped
        || (AliasOf(repositoryFullName) is { } alias && RepositoryScope.Contains(alias, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase));

    /// <summary>A repository's label filter, empty for none — read from the registry on
    /// every render, so a filter changed in Settings narrows the rows already read.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<string> LabelFilterOf(string repositoryFullName) =>
        _gitHub?.Repositories.FirstOrDefault(candidate =>
            string.Equals(candidate.FullName, repositoryFullName, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))?.PullRequestLabels ?? [];

    private bool PassesLabels(string repositoryFullName, IReadOnlyList<string> labels) =>
        PullRequestLabelFilter.Passes(labels, LabelFilterOf(repositoryFullName), pinned: false);

    /// <summary>The in-scope repositories with a label filter, by alias, each with the
    /// labels it lets through.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<(string Repository, IReadOnlyList<string> Labels)> LabelFiltered =>
        _gitHub is null
            ? []
            : [.. _gitHub.Repositories
                .Where(repository => repository.PullRequestLabels.Count > 0 && InScope(repository.FullName))
                .Select(repository => (RepositoryLabel(repository.FullName), repository.PullRequestLabels))];

    private string LabelFilterSentence =>
        string.Join(" ", LabelFiltered.Select(filter => $"Label filter on {filter.Repository}: {string.Join(" or ", filter.Labels)}."));

    /// <summary>The pull request as the shell's task relation asks about it, with the
    /// session this pane matched it to.</summary>
    private PullRequestTaskSubject TaskSubject(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) =>
        PullRequestTaskSubject.From(pull, SessionFor(pull.Url, pull.HeadRefName, pull.RepositoryFullName)?.Id);

    private PullRequestTaskSubject TaskSubject(GitHubMergedPullRequest pull) =>
        PullRequestTaskSubject.From(pull, SessionFor(pull.Url, pull.HeadRefName, pull.RepositoryFullName)?.Id);

    /// <summary>Mine: the reader opened it, or it is related to one of their tasks.</summary>
    private bool IsMine(bool viewerDidAuthor, Func<PullRequestTaskSubject> subject) =>
        viewerDidAuthor || PullRequestTask?.Invoke(subject(), true) is not null;

    /// <summary>Everything the open view can draw: the open list, plus each pinned pull
    /// request it does not hold — merged, closed, or past its fifty — while it is
    /// still pinned. Newest update first, as read.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<GitHubOpenPullRequest> OpenRows
    {
        get
        {
            if (_pinned.PullRequests.Count == 0) return _listing.PullRequests;

            var listed = _listing.PullRequests.Select(Key).ToHashSet(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
            return [.. _listing.PullRequests, .. _pinned.PullRequests.Where(pull => !listed.Contains(Key(pull)) && IsPinned(pull))];
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The scope decides which repositories exist here at all.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<GitHubOpenPullRequest> InScopeRows => [.. OpenRows.Where(pull => InScope(pull.RepositoryFullName))];

    /// <summary>What the label filters leave of the scope.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<GitHubOpenPullRequest> LabelledRows => [.. InScopeRows.Where(pull => PassesLabels(pull.RepositoryFullName, pull.Labels))];

    /// <summary>The scope, the label filters, then whose — and every pinned pull
    /// request whatever they say. The lane is not one of them: the tiles count what
    /// this leaves, and the board narrows it.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<GitHubOpenPullRequest> Visible =>
        [.. OpenRows.Where(pull => IsPinned(pull)
            || (InScope(pull.RepositoryFullName)
                && PassesLabels(pull.RepositoryFullName, pull.Labels)
                && (!_mine || IsMine(pull.ViewerDidAuthor, () => TaskSubject(pull)))))];

    private PullRequestStacks? _stacks;
    private (GitHubPullRequestListing Listing, GitHubPullRequestListing Pinned, string Scope, int Pins) _stacksOf;

    /// <summary>The stacks among the open rows of every author in scope, and the pinned
    /// open ones, derived once per read, scope and pin rather than once per row that
    /// asks. A merged or closed pinned pull request is in no stack.</summary>
    private PullRequestStacks Stacks
    {
        get
        {
            var of = (_listing, _pinned, ScopeLabel, _pinsVersion);
            if (_stacks is null || _stacksOf != of)
            {
                _stacks = PullRequestStacks.Of(OpenRows.Where(pull => pull.IsOpen && (IsPinned(pull) || InScope(pull.RepositoryFullName))));
                _stacksOf = of;
            }

            return _stacks;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The pinned rows first, newest update first; then the rest, with each
    /// stack gathered into one tree, bottom first, placed where the latest update
    /// among its shown rows puts it, and every other row in the newest-update-first
    /// order it was read in. A pinned row in a stack sits with the pins. The board
    /// then deals these into their lanes, each keeping this order.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<GitHubOpenPullRequest> Ordered
    {
        get
        {
            var stacks = Stacks;
            var visible = Visible;
            var pinned = visible.Where(IsPinned).OrderByDescending(pull => pull.UpdatedAt).ToList();
            var rest = visible.Where(pull => !IsPinned(pull)).ToList();

            if (stacks.Stacks.Count == 0) return [.. pinned, .. rest];

            var shown = rest.ToHashSet();
            var trees = stacks.Stacks
                .Select(stack => (IReadOnlyList<GitHubOpenPullRequest>)[.. stack.Members.Where(shown.Contains)])
                .Where(rows => rows.Count > 0);
            var singles = rest
                .Where(pull => stacks.StackOf(pull) is null)
                .Select(pull => (IReadOnlyList<GitHubOpenPullRequest>)[pull]);

            return [.. pinned, .. singles.Concat(trees)
                .OrderByDescending(rows => rows.Max(pull => pull.UpdatedAt))
                .SelectMany(rows => rows)];
        }
    }

    private IReadOnlyList<GitHubMergedPullRequest> MergedRows => (_merged ?? GitHubMergedPullRequestListing.Empty).PullRequests;

    /// <summary>The merged view's rows, narrowed the same ways. Newest merge first, as
    /// the adapter ordered them.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<GitHubMergedPullRequest> MergedInScopeRows =>
        [.. MergedRows.Where(pull => InScope(pull.RepositoryFullName))];

    private IReadOnlyList<GitHubMergedPullRequest> MergedLabelledRows =>
        [.. MergedInScopeRows.Where(pull => PassesLabels(pull.RepositoryFullName, pull.Labels))];

    private IReadOnlyList<GitHubMergedPullRequest> MergedVisible =>
        [.. MergedRows.Where(pull => IsPinned(pull.RepositoryFullName, pull.Number)
            || (InScope(pull.RepositoryFullName)
                && PassesLabels(pull.RepositoryFullName, pull.Labels)
                && (!_mine || IsMine(pull.ViewerDidAuthor, () => TaskSubject(pull)))))];

    /// <summary>
    /// The view's counts: everything read, what the scope leaves, what the label
    /// filters leave of that, what Mine leaves of that, and the total the badge
    /// counts against — the scope's rows plus the pinned ones outside it, so a pin
    /// never makes the badge say more shown than there are.
    /// </summary>
    private (int Read, int InScope, int Labelled, int Shown, int Total) Counts =>
        Merged
            ? (MergedRows.Count,
               MergedInScopeRows.Count,
               MergedLabelledRows.Count,
               MergedVisible.Count,
               MergedRows.Count(pull => InScope(pull.RepositoryFullName) || IsPinned(pull.RepositoryFullName, pull.Number)))
            : (OpenRows.Count,
               InScopeRows.Count,
               LabelledRows.Count,
               Visible.Count,
               OpenRows.Count(pull => InScope(pull.RepositoryFullName) || IsPinned(pull)));

    /// <summary>Every repository a read of this view could not complete — the pinned
    /// read's too on the open view — each named once.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<GitHubRepositoryFailure> Failures =>
        Merged
            ? (_merged ?? GitHubMergedPullRequestListing.Empty).Failures
            : [.. _listing.Failures.Concat(_pinned.Failures)
                .DistinctBy(failure => (failure.RepositoryFullName.ToUpperInvariant(), failure.Message))];

    /// <summary>The window in words, from the adapter's own constant so the sentence
    /// cannot drift from what was read.</summary>
    private static string Window => $"the last {GitHubIntegration.RecentlyMergedWindow.TotalDays:0} days";

    private string CountLabel
    {
        get
        {
            var (_, _, _, shown, total) = Counts;
            var noun = total == 1 ? "pull request" : "pull requests";
            if (Merged) noun = $"merged {noun}";

            return shown == total ? $"{total} {noun}" : $"{shown} of {total} {noun}";
        }
    }

    private string Subtitle
    {
        get
        {
            if (!Configured) return "The open pull requests of the repositories registered in Settings.";

            var reading = Merged
                ? $"The pull requests merged in {Window} in every registered repository, most recent merge first."
                : "The open pull requests of every registered repository, most recently updated first — up to fifty per repository.";

            var scoped = Scoped ? $"{reading} Narrowed to {ScopeLabel}." : reading;
            var labels = LabelFilterSentence;

            return labels.Length == 0 ? scoped : $"{scoped} {labels}";
        }
    }

    private string EmptyMessage
    {
        get
        {
            var (read, inScope, labelled, _, _) = Counts;

            return Merged
                ? read == 0
                    ? $"No pull requests merged in {Window}."
                    : Scoped && inScope == 0
                        ? $"No pull requests merged in {ScopeLabel} in {Window}."
                        : labelled == 0
                            ? "None of the recently merged pull requests carries a label the filter asks for."
                            : "None of the recently merged pull requests is yours."
                : read == 0
                    ? "No open pull requests."
                    : Scoped && inScope == 0
                        ? $"No open pull requests in {ScopeLabel}."
                        : labelled == 0
                            ? "None of the open pull requests carries a label the filter asks for."
                            : "None of the open pull requests is yours.";
        }
    }

    private string EmptyDescription
    {
        get
        {
            var (read, inScope, labelled, _, _) = Counts;

            return read == 0
                ? Merged
                    ? "Nothing was merged in the repositories that could be read."
                    : "Nothing is open in the repositories that could be read."
                : Scoped && inScope == 0
                    ? "Clear the repository scope in the header to see every repository's."
                    : labelled == 0
                        ? $"{LabelFilterSentence} Change it on the repository's card in Settings."
                        : Merged
                            ? $"Choose Everyone's to see the {labelled} that others opened."
                            : $"Choose Everyone's to see the {labelled} opened by somebody else.";
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Whether a lane is what emptied the list: something is shown before the
    /// lane narrows it, and nothing after.</summary>
    private bool LaneEmptied => !Merged && _lane is not null && Visible.Count > 0;

    private string ListEmptyTitle => LaneEmptied && _lane is { } lane ? $"Nothing in {LaneLabel(lane)}." : EmptyMessage;

    private string ListEmptyDescription => LaneEmptied ? "Press the tile again to see every lane." : EmptyDescription;

    private string FailureMessage =>
        string.Join(" ", Failures.Select(failure => $"Couldn't read {failure.RepositoryFullName}: {failure.Message.TrimEnd('.')}."))
        + " Every other repository below is complete.";

    private static string TruncatedMessage(IReadOnlyList<string> repositories) =>
        $"Only the {GitHubClient.MergedPageSize * GitHubClient.MergedPageCap} most recently updated merged pull requests "
        + $"of {string.Join(", ", repositories)} were read, so some of what merged there in {Window} is missing.";

    // --- The board ----------------------------------------------------------------

    /// <summary>One row of the list, from either view: an open (or pinned) pull
    /// request with its verdict and its place in a stack, or a merged one.</summary>
    /// <param name="Verdict">Null only for a pinned pull request closed without
    /// merging.</param>
    /// <param name="Parent">The open pull request it waits on, for an open one in a
    /// stack above its bottom.</param>
    /// <param name="Depth">Its level in its stack, for an open one in a stack that is
    /// not pinned — a pinned one sits with the pins rather than in its tree.</param>
    private sealed record BoardRow(
        string Key,
        GitHubOpenPullRequest? Open,
        GitHubMergedPullRequest? MergedPull,
        PullRequestVerdict? Verdict,
        GitHubOpenPullRequest? Parent,
        int? Depth,
        bool Pinned)
    {
        public string RepositoryFullName => Open?.RepositoryFullName ?? MergedPull!.RepositoryFullName;

        public int Number => Open?.Number ?? MergedPull!.Number;

        public string Title => Open?.Title ?? MergedPull!.Title;

        public string HeadRefName => Open?.HeadRefName ?? MergedPull!.HeadRefName;

        public string BaseRefName => Open?.BaseRefName ?? MergedPull!.BaseRefName;

        public string Url => Open?.Url ?? MergedPull!.Url;

        public string? AuthorLogin => Open?.AuthorLogin ?? MergedPull!.AuthorLogin;

        /// <summary>Indented under the one it waits on.</summary>
        public bool Stacked => Depth is > 0;
    }

    /// <summary>A heading and its rows: a lane, the pins, or the merged window.</summary>
    private sealed record BoardGroup(string Slug, string Label, IReadOnlyList<BoardRow> Rows);

    /// <summary>A lane's tile: how many are in it and, in a line, why.</summary>
    private sealed record LaneTile(PullRequestLane Lane, int Total, string Reasons);

    /// <summary>What one render draws: the groups, the tiles, and the row the detail
    /// is about — derived once per render rather than once per element that asks.</summary>
    private sealed record Board(IReadOnlyList<BoardGroup> Groups, IReadOnlyList<LaneTile> Lanes, BoardRow? Selected);

    /// <summary>The open view: tiles counted over every row the filters leave, the
    /// pins first, then a group per lane that has rows, in lane order.</summary>
    private Board OpenBoard()
    {
        var stacks = Stacks;
        var rows = Ordered.Select(pull => OpenRow(pull, stacks)).ToList();

        var tiles = Lanes
            .Select(lane =>
            {
                var inLane = rows.Where(row => row.Verdict?.Lane == lane).ToList();
                return new LaneTile(lane, inLane.Count, LaneReasons(lane, inLane));
            })
            .ToList();

        var shown = rows.Where(row => row.Pinned || _lane is null || row.Verdict?.Lane == _lane).ToList();

        var groups = new List<BoardGroup>();
        var pinned = shown.Where(row => row.Pinned).ToList();
        if (pinned.Count > 0) groups.Add(new BoardGroup("pinned", "Pinned", pinned));

        foreach (var lane in Lanes)
        {
            var inLane = shown.Where(row => !row.Pinned && row.Verdict?.Lane == lane).ToList();
            if (inLane.Count > 0) groups.Add(new BoardGroup(LaneSlug(lane), LaneLabel(lane), inLane));
        }

        return new Board(groups, tiles, SelectedOf(groups));
    }

    /// <summary>The merged view: one group, the window it was read for, and no tiles —
    /// a merged pull request is in no lane.</summary>
    private Board MergedBoard()
    {
        var rows = MergedVisible
            .Select(pull => new BoardRow(
                Key(pull.RepositoryFullName, pull.Number), null, pull, PullRequestVerdict.Of(pull), null, null,
                IsPinned(pull.RepositoryFullName, pull.Number)))
            .ToList();

        IReadOnlyList<BoardGroup> groups = rows.Count == 0
            ? []
            : [new BoardGroup("merged", $"Last {GitHubIntegration.RecentlyMergedWindow.TotalDays:0} days", rows)];

        return new Board(groups, [], SelectedOf(groups));
    }

    private BoardRow OpenRow(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull, PullRequestStacks stacks)
    {
        var pinned = IsPinned(pull);
        var parent = pull.IsOpen ? stacks.ParentOf(pull) : null;

        return new BoardRow(
            Key(pull),
            pull,
            null,
            PullRequestVerdict.Of(pull, parent, pull.CanRerunFailed),
            parent,
            pinned ? null : stacks.DepthOf(pull),
            pinned);
    }

    /// <summary>The pick where it is still shown, else the first row shown.</summary>
    private BoardRow? SelectedOf(IReadOnlyList<BoardGroup> groups)
    {
        var shown = groups.SelectMany(group => group.Rows).ToList();
        return shown.FirstOrDefault(row => string.Equals(row.Key, _selected, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
            ?? shown.FirstOrDefault();
    }

    /// <summary>A tile's line: what its pull requests are waiting on, one reason per
    /// kind of verdict, so the count beside it has a reason. By kind rather than by the
    /// chip's label, which carries a count — two pull requests failing one and two
    /// checks are one reason, not two.</summary>
    private static string LaneReasons(PullRequestLane lane, IReadOnlyList<BoardRow> rows) =>
        rows.Count == 0
            ? "Nothing here"
            : lane switch
            {
                PullRequestLane.ReadyToMerge => "Nothing in the way",
                PullRequestLane.Drafts => rows.Any(row => row.Parent is not null) ? "Includes a stacked branch" : "Not ready for review",
                PullRequestLane.NeedsYou or PullRequestLane.Waiting =>
                    string.Join(" · ", rows.Select(row => row.Verdict!.Kind).Distinct().Select(ReasonWord))
            };

    /// <summary>A verdict kind as a tile names it.</summary>
    private static string ReasonWord(PullRequestVerdictKind kind) => kind switch
    {
        PullRequestVerdictKind.Conflicts => "conflicts",
        PullRequestVerdictKind.FailingChecks => "failing checks",
        PullRequestVerdictKind.ChangesRequested => "changes requested",
        PullRequestVerdictKind.Behind => "behind",
        PullRequestVerdictKind.Draft => "draft",
        PullRequestVerdictKind.ChecksRunning => "checks running",
        PullRequestVerdictKind.ReviewRequired => "review required",
        PullRequestVerdictKind.Ready => "ready to merge",
        PullRequestVerdictKind.Merged => "merged"
    };

    private static string LaneLabel(PullRequestLane lane) => lane switch
    {
        PullRequestLane.NeedsYou => "Needs you",
        PullRequestLane.ReadyToMerge => "Ready to merge",
        PullRequestLane.Waiting => "Waiting",
        PullRequestLane.Drafts => "Drafts"
    };

    private static string LaneSlug(PullRequestLane lane) => lane switch
    {
        PullRequestLane.NeedsYou => "needs-you",
        PullRequestLane.ReadyToMerge => "ready",
        PullRequestLane.Waiting => "waiting",
        PullRequestLane.Drafts => "drafts"
    };

    /// <summary>The tone a lane's tile marks itself with — the tone its worst verdict
    /// wears.</summary>
    private static string LaneTone(PullRequestLane lane) => lane switch
    {
        PullRequestLane.NeedsYou => "fault",
        PullRequestLane.ReadyToMerge => "settled",
        PullRequestLane.Waiting => "live",
        PullRequestLane.Drafts => "quiet"
    };

    /// <summary>The badge tone of a verdict, by the scale's own names; a pull request
    /// closed without merging is out of force and wears archived.</summary>
    private static string ToneSlug(PullRequestVerdict? verdict) => verdict?.Tone switch
    {
        PullRequestTone.Quiet => "quiet",
        PullRequestTone.Live => "live",
        PullRequestTone.Alert => "alert",
        PullRequestTone.Fault => "fault",
        PullRequestTone.Settled => "settled",
        null => "archived"
    };

    private static string VerdictLabel(PullRequestVerdict? verdict) => verdict?.Label ?? "Closed";

    private static string RowClass(BoardRow row)
    {
        var classes = "pull-requests-row";
        if (row.Stacked) classes += " pull-requests-row--stacked";
        if (row.Open is { IsOpen: false }) classes += " pull-requests-row--closed";
        return classes;
    }

    /// <summary>What a driver reads off a row: which pull request, whether it is
    /// pinned, its level in a stack, and its lane — and the indent the stack gives it.</summary>
    private static IReadOnlyDictionary<string, object> RowAttributes(BoardRow row)
    {
        var attributes = new Dictionary<string, object> { ["data-pull-request"] = row.Key };

        if (row.Pinned) attributes["data-pinned"] = "true";
        if (row.Depth is { } depth) attributes["data-stack-depth"] = depth.ToString(System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
        if (row.Verdict?.Lane is { } lane) attributes["data-lane"] = LaneSlug(lane);
        if (row.Stacked) attributes["style"] = $"--chain-depth: {row.Depth!.Value.ToString(System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)}";

        return attributes;
    }

    private string RepositoryLabel(string repositoryFullName) => AliasOf(repositoryFullName) ?? repositoryFullName;

    /// <summary>The repository's alias with its identity mark where the host placed
    /// one: the hue down its leading edge, as on the session list.</summary>
    private string RepositoryClass(string stem, string repositoryFullName)
    {
        var colour = RepositoryColour?.Invoke(repositoryFullName);

        return colour is null ? stem : $"{stem} repo-mark repo-mark--{colour}";
    }

    /// <summary>How long ago an open pull request last moved, against the pane's clock.</summary>
    private string? UpdatedAgo(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) =>
        pull.UpdatedAt is { } at ? Backlog.UI.Components.Shell.SyncStatusLine.Relative(_clock.GetUtcNow() - at) : null;

    /// <summary>How long before the reading it was merged, coarsely — the exact
    /// moment is in <see cref="MergedTitle"/>.</summary>
    private string MergedAgo(GitHubMergedPullRequest pull) =>
        Backlog.UI.Components.Shell.SyncStatusLine.Relative(_mergedReadAt - pull.MergedAt);

    /// <summary>Local time, because a reader matching a merge against their own day is
    /// not thinking in UTC; the author too, which the row does not say.</summary>
    private static string MergedTitle(GitHubMergedPullRequest pull)
    {
        var when = $"Merged {pull.MergedAt.ToLocalTime():ddd d MMM yyyy HH:mm}.";
        return pull.AuthorLogin is { } author ? $"{when} Opened by {author}." : when;
    }

    /// <summary>When a pinned pull request merged or closed, in local time.</summary>
    private static string? ClosedTitle(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) =>
        (pull.IsMerged ? pull.MergedAt ?? pull.ClosedAt : pull.ClosedAt) is { } at
            ? $"{(pull.IsMerged ? "Merged" : "Closed")} {at.ToLocalTime():ddd d MMM yyyy HH:mm}."
            : null;

    private static string ChecksTitle(GitHubCheckCounts counts) =>
        $"{counts.Passed} of the head commit's {counts.Total} checks passed, {counts.Failed} failed, {counts.Pending} still running or waiting.";

    /// <summary>The meter's three widths, as the counts themselves: each part grows by
    /// its share, so the bar needs no arithmetic here.</summary>
    private static string MeterStyle(GitHubCheckCounts counts) =>
        string.Create(
            System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture,
            $"--checks-passed: {counts.Passed}; --checks-failed: {counts.Failed}; --checks-running: {counts.Pending}");

    /// <summary>The pull request as the Integrations family draws one, on the detail's
    /// head: an anchor to GitHub wearing its state as its colour, with the state's
    /// words in its title and an sr-only span.</summary>
    private static IntegrationLinkRef Link(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) =>
        IntegrationLinkRef.PullRequest(
            pull.Url,
            "Open on GitHub",
            pull.State switch
            {
                GitHubItemState.Merged => IntegrationArtifactState.Merged,
                GitHubItemState.Closed => IntegrationArtifactState.Closed,
                GitHubItemState.Draft => IntegrationArtifactState.Draft,
                _ => IntegrationArtifactState.Open
            },
            pull.Title,
            pull.Url);

    private static IntegrationLinkRef MergedLink(GitHubMergedPullRequest pull) =>
        IntegrationLinkRef.PullRequest(pull.Url, "Open on GitHub", IntegrationArtifactState.Merged, pull.Title, pull.Url);

    // --- A row --------------------------------------------------------------------

    /// <summary>
    /// One row: the repository's identity edge and alias, the number, the verdict
    /// chip, the title, the head branch and its age, and the checks meter. Nothing in
    /// it is a control — the row is the button — so the pin and the links live in
    /// the detail.
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment RowBody(BoardRow row) =>
        @<text>
            <span class="pull-requests-row__top">
                <span class="@RepositoryClass("pull-requests-row__repository", row.RepositoryFullName)" title="@row.RepositoryFullName" data-testid="pull-request-repository">@RepositoryLabel(row.RepositoryFullName)</span>
                <span class="pull-requests-row__number">#@row.Number</span>
                <Badge Kind="tone"
                       Slug="@ToneSlug(row.Verdict)"
                       Title="@(row.Open is { IsOpen: false } closed ? ClosedTitle(closed) : null)"
                       CssClass="pull-requests-row__verdict"
                       TestId="pull-request-verdict">@VerdictLabel(row.Verdict)</Badge>
            </span>
            <span class="pull-requests-row__title">@row.Title</span>
            <span class="pull-requests-row__meta">
                <span class="pull-requests-row__branch" title="@($"{row.HeadRefName} → {row.BaseRefName}")">@row.HeadRefName</span>
                @if (row.MergedPull is { } merged)
                {
                    <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                    <span class="pull-requests-row__age">
                        <span title="@MergedTitle(merged)" data-testid="pull-request-merged-at">@MergedAgo(merged)</span>
                        @if (merged.MergedByLogin is { } merger)
                        {
                            @(" · by ")<span data-testid="pull-request-merged-by">@merger</span>
                        }
                    </span>
                }
                else if (row.Open is { } pull)
                {
                    @if (UpdatedAgo(pull) is { } ago)
                    {
                        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                        <span class="pull-requests-row__age">@ago</span>
                    }
                    @if (pull.IsOpen && pull.CheckCounts is { Total: > 0 } counts)
                    {
                        @* GitHub's "8/9", drawn: passed, failed and running as three
                           widths, with the words beside it and the exact counts in
                           the title, so the bar is never the only carrier. *@
                        <span class="pull-request-checks-meter"
                              title="@ChecksTitle(counts)"
                              style="@MeterStyle(counts)"
                              data-testid="pull-request-checks-meter">
                            <span class="pull-request-checks-meter__bar" aria-hidden="true">
                                <span class="pull-request-checks-meter__passed"></span>
                                <span class="pull-request-checks-meter__failed"></span>
                                <span class="pull-request-checks-meter__running"></span>
                            </span>
                            <span class="pull-request-checks-meter__words">@($"{counts.Passed}/{counts.Total}")<span class="sr-only"> checks passed</span></span>
                        </span>
                    }
                }
            </span>
            @if (row.Stacked && row.Parent is { } parent)
            {
                @* The one place the row says what it waits on: a reader sees it
                   hang under its parent, and the words say why. *@
                <span class="pull-requests-row__waits"
                      title="@($"It targets {parent.HeadRefName}, so merge #{parent.Number} first.")"
                      data-testid="pull-request-waits-on">↳ Waits on #@parent.Number, merge that first</span>
            }
        </text>;

    // --- The detail -----------------------------------------------------------------

    /// <summary>The detail of the picked pull request: its head, the verdict and its
    /// acts, and — for one still open — what GitHub gates the merge on, its checks and
    /// its stack; then the task and the session it came from.</summary>
    private RenderFragment Detail(BoardRow row) =>
        @<aside class="pull-request-detail" aria-label="Selected pull request" data-testid="pull-request-detail" data-pull-request="@row.Key">
            <header class="pull-request-detail__head">
                <div class="pull-request-detail__line">
                    <span class="@RepositoryClass("pull-request-detail__repository", row.RepositoryFullName)" title="@row.RepositoryFullName">@RepositoryLabel(row.RepositoryFullName)</span>
                    <span class="pull-request-detail__number">#@row.Number</span>
                    <span class="pull-request-detail__byline">@Byline(row)</span>
                    <span class="pull-request-detail__links">
                        @if (row.Open is { } open)
                        {
                            <IntegrationLink Link="@Link(open)"
                                             StateAsInk="true"
                                             ShowTitle="false"
                                             CssClass="pull-request-detail__github"
                                             TestId="pull-request-link"
                                             StateTestId="pull-request-state" />
                        }
                        else if (row.MergedPull is { } merged)
                        {
                            <IntegrationLink Link="@MergedLink(merged)"
                                             StateAsInk="true"
                                             ShowTitle="false"
                                             CssClass="pull-request-detail__github"
                                             TestId="pull-request-link"
                                             StateTestId="pull-request-state" />
                        }
                        @PinToggle(row.RepositoryFullName, row.Number)
                    </span>
                </div>
                <h3 class="pull-request-detail__title">@row.Title</h3>
                <p class="pull-request-detail__branches" title="@($"{row.HeadRefName} → {row.BaseRefName}")">@($"{row.HeadRefName} → {row.BaseRefName}")</p>
            </header>

            @Banner(row)

            @if (row.Open is { IsOpen: true } pull)
            {
                <div class="pull-request-detail__facts">
                    <section class="pull-request-detail__section" aria-label="Merge readiness">
                        <h4 class="pull-request-detail__heading">Merge readiness</h4>
                        <ul class="pull-request-readiness" data-testid="pull-request-readiness">
                            @foreach (var line in Readiness(pull))
                            {
                                <li class="@($"pull-request-readiness__line pull-request-readiness__line--{line.State}")"
                                    data-line="@line.Slug"
                                    data-state="@line.State">
                                    <span class="pull-request-readiness__mark" aria-hidden="true">@ReadinessMark(line.State)</span>
                                    <span class="pull-request-readiness__label">@line.Label</span>
                                    <span class="pull-request-readiness__words">@line.Words<span class="sr-only">@ReadinessWord(line.State)</span></span>
                                </li>
                            }
                        </ul>
                    </section>

                    <section class="pull-request-detail__section" aria-label="Checks">
                        <h4 class="pull-request-detail__heading">
                            Checks
                            @if (pull.CheckCounts is { Total: > 0 } counts)
                            {
                                <span class="pull-request-detail__tally">@($"{counts.Passed}/{counts.Total} passed")</span>
                            }
                        </h4>
                        @ChecksList(pull)
                    </section>
                </div>

                @if (Stacks.StackOf(pull) is { } stack)
                {
                    <section class="pull-request-detail__section" aria-label="Stack" data-testid="pull-request-stack">
                        <h4 class="pull-request-detail__heading">Stack · merges bottom first</h4>
                        <ol class="pull-request-stack">
                            @foreach (var member in stack.Members)
                            {
                                var current = member == pull;
                                <li class="@(current ? "pull-request-stack__member pull-request-stack__member--current" : "pull-request-stack__member")"
                                    aria-current="@(current ? "true" : null)"
                                    data-pull-request="@Key(member)">
                                    <span class="pull-request-stack__number">#@member.Number</span>
                                    <span class="pull-request-stack__title">@member.Title</span>
                                    <Badge Kind="tone" Slug="@ToneSlug(MemberVerdict(member))">@VerdictLabel(MemberVerdict(member))</Badge>
                                </li>
                            }
                        </ol>
                    </section>
                }
            }

            @* The way back to the work: the task the pull request belongs to and the
               session that made it, each said in a sentence when nothing matched
               rather than left as a blank card. *@
            <div class="pull-request-detail__cards">
                <Card Title="Task" Compact="true" CssClass="pull-request-detail__card">
                    @if (TaskFor(row) is { } task)
                    {
                        <IntegrationLink Link="@TaskLink(task)"
                                         ShowTitle="false"
                                         OnOpen="@TaskOpener(task)"
                                         TestId="pull-request-task" />
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <p class="pull-request-detail__unmatched" data-testid="pull-request-no-task">No task names this pull request.</p>
                    }
                </Card>
                <Card Title="Session" Compact="true" CssClass="pull-request-detail__card">
                    @if (SessionFor(row.Url, row.HeadRefName, row.RepositoryFullName) is { } session)
                    {
                        <IntegrationLink Link="@SessionLink(session)"
                                         ShowTitle="false"
                                         OnOpen="SessionOpener"
                                         TestId="pull-request-session" />
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <p class="pull-request-detail__unmatched" data-testid="pull-request-no-session">No session matched this pull request.</p>
                    }
                </Card>
            </div>
        </aside>;

    /// <summary>A stack member's verdict, read the way its own row reads it.</summary>
    private PullRequestVerdict? MemberVerdict(GitHubOpenPullRequest member) =>
        PullRequestVerdict.Of(member, Stacks.ParentOf(member), member.CanRerunFailed);

    /// <summary>Who opened it and how long ago it moved — or merged, for a merged one.</summary>
    private string Byline(BoardRow row)
    {
        var age = row.MergedPull is { } merged ? $"merged {MergedAgo(merged)}" : row.Open is { } open ? UpdatedAgo(open) : null;
        var by = row.AuthorLogin is { } author ? $"by {author}" : null;

        return string.Join(" · ", new[] { by, age }.Where(part => part is not null));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The verdict, in its tone: the chip, the headline, the one-sentence reason, and
    /// the acts that fit — the secondary before the primary, so the primary sits at
    /// the end of the line where the eye finishes. A pull request closed without
    /// merging has no verdict; the banner says so in the archived tone, with no act.
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment Banner(BoardRow row) => __builder =>
    {
        var verdict = row.Verdict;
        var tone = ToneSlug(verdict);
        var headline = verdict?.Headline ?? "Closed without merging";
        var reason = verdict?.Reason ?? "Nothing is left to do from here.";
        IReadOnlyList<(PullRequestAct Act, bool Primary)> acts = row.Open is { } pull ? ActsFor(pull, verdict) : [];

        <div class="@($"pull-request-banner pull-request-banner--{tone}")"
             data-testid="pull-request-banner"
             data-verdict="@(verdict?.Kind.ToString() ?? "Closed")">
            <div class="pull-request-banner__text">
                <Badge Kind="tone" Slug="@tone">@VerdictLabel(verdict)</Badge>
                <p class="pull-request-banner__headline">@headline</p>
                <p class="pull-request-banner__reason">@reason</p>
            </div>
            @if (acts.Count > 0 && row.Open is { } open)
            {
                <div class="pull-request-banner__acts">
                    @foreach (var (act, primary) in acts)
                    {
                        @ActButton(open, act, primary)
                    }
                </div>
            }
        </div>
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// The acts the banner offers, secondary first. The verdict's own — plus Cancel
    /// auto-merge wherever GitHub already holds an auto-merge and the verdict offers no
    /// merge act to withdraw it with: a draft, a branch in conflict, a stacked pull
    /// request. Withdrawing undoes a request rather than making one, so nothing the
    /// verdict waits on is a reason to hide it.
    /// </summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<(PullRequestAct Act, bool Primary)> ActsFor(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull, PullRequestVerdict? verdict)
    {
        if (verdict is null || !pull.IsOpen) return [];

        var acts = new List<(PullRequestAct Act, bool Primary)>();
        if (verdict.SecondaryAct is { } secondary) acts.Add((secondary, false));
        if (verdict.PrimaryAct is { } primary) acts.Add((primary, true));

        if (!acts.Any(entry => IsMergeAct(entry.Act)) && OfferedMergeFor(pull) is PullRequestMerge.CancelAutoMerge)
        {
            acts.Insert(0, (PullRequestAct.MergeWhenReady, false));
        }

        return acts;
    }

    private static bool IsMergeAct(PullRequestAct act) => act is PullRequestAct.Merge or PullRequestAct.MergeWhenReady;

    /// <summary>One act as its control. The two that only go and look are links to
    /// GitHub; the rest are the pane's own act methods. A merge act becomes whichever
    /// merge GitHub would accept — and nothing where it would accept none.</summary>
    private RenderFragment ActButton(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull, PullRequestAct act, bool primary) => __builder =>
    {
        var variant = primary ? ButtonVariant.Primary : ButtonVariant.Secondary;
        var busy = Busy(pull);

        switch (act)
        {
            case PullRequestAct.OpenOnGitHub:
                <AppButton Href="@pull.Url" Variant="variant" TestId="pull-request-open-on-github">Open on GitHub</AppButton>
                break;
            case PullRequestAct.OpenReviewOnGitHub:
                <AppButton Href="@($"{pull.Url}/files")" Variant="variant" TestId="pull-request-open-review">Open review on GitHub</AppButton>
                break;
            case PullRequestAct.RerunFailed:
                <AppButton Variant="variant" Disabled="@busy" TestId="pull-request-rerun-failed" OnClick="() => RerunFailedAsync(pull)">Re-run failed</AppButton>
                break;
            case PullRequestAct.UpdateBranch:
                <AppButton Variant="variant" Disabled="@busy" TestId="pull-request-update-branch" OnClick="() => UpdateBranchAsync(pull)">Update branch</AppButton>
                break;
            case PullRequestAct.ReadyForReview:
                <AppButton Variant="variant" Disabled="@busy" TestId="pull-request-ready" OnClick="() => MarkReadyAsync(pull)">Ready for review</AppButton>
                break;
            case PullRequestAct.MergeWhenReady:
            case PullRequestAct.Merge:
                if (OfferedMergeFor(pull) is { } merge)
                {
                    <AppButton Variant="variant" Disabled="@busy" TestId="pull-request-merge" OnClick="() => MergeAsync(pull)">@MergeLabel(merge)</AppButton>
                }
                break;
        }
    };

    /// <summary>One of the four things GitHub gates a merge on, in words.</summary>
    /// <param name="State"><c>ok</c>, <c>waiting</c> or <c>failing</c>.</param>
    private sealed record ReadinessLine(string Slug, string Label, string State, string Words);

    private const string Ok = "ok";
    private const string Waiting = "waiting";
    private const string Failing = "failing";

    /// <summary>Checks, review, up to date, mergeable — each ok, waiting or failing,
    /// said in words. Nothing here is a verdict: these are the facts the verdict was
    /// ranked from, so a reader can see what else stands in the way.</summary>
    private static IReadOnlyList<ReadinessLine> Readiness(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull)
    {
        var baseRef = pull.BaseRefName;

        var (checksState, checksWords) = pull.CheckCounts switch
        {
            { Failed: > 0 } counts => (Failing, $"{counts.Failed} failing"),
            { Pending: > 0 } counts => (Waiting, $"{counts.Pending} running"),
            { Total: > 0 } counts => (Ok, $"{counts.Total}/{counts.Total} passed"),
            _ => pull.Checks switch
            {
                GitHubCheckState.Failing => (Failing, "Failing"),
                GitHubCheckState.Pending => (Waiting, "Pending"),
                GitHubCheckState.Passing => (Ok, "Passing"),
                GitHubCheckState.None => (Waiting, "None reported yet")
            }
        };

        var reviews = pull.Reviews;
        var (reviewState, reviewWords) =
            reviews.Decision == GitHubReviewDecision.ChangesRequested || reviews.ChangesRequested > 0 ? (Failing, "Changes requested")
            : reviews.Approvals > 0 ? (Ok, reviews.Approvals == 1 ? "1 approval" : $"{reviews.Approvals} approvals")
            : pull.IsDraft ? (Waiting, "Not requested (draft)")
            : reviews.Decision == GitHubReviewDecision.ReviewRequired ? (Waiting, "Approval required")
            : (Ok, "No review required");

        var (behindState, behindWords) =
            pull.BehindBy is > 0 and var behind ? (Waiting, behind == 1 ? $"1 commit behind {baseRef}" : $"{behind} commits behind {baseRef}")
            : pull.IsBehind ? (Waiting, $"Behind {baseRef}")
            : pull.BehindBy == 0 ? (Ok, $"With {baseRef}")
            : pull.IsCrossRepository ? (Ok, "Not compared")
            : (Ok, $"With {baseRef}");

        var (mergeableState, mergeableWords) = pull.HasConflicts ? (Failing, $"Conflicts with {baseRef}") : (Ok, "No conflicts");

        return
        [
            new("checks", "Checks", checksState, checksWords),
            new("review", "Review", reviewState, reviewWords),
            new("up-to-date", "Up to date", behindState, behindWords),
            new("mergeable", "Mergeable", mergeableState, mergeableWords)
        ];
    }

    /// <summary>A glyph per state, beside the words: three shapes, so the colour on
    /// the line is never the only thing telling them apart.</summary>
    private static string ReadinessMark(string state) => state switch
    {
        Ok => "✓",
        Failing => "✕",
        _ => "○"
    };

    private static string ReadinessWord(string state) => state switch
    {
        Ok => " (ok)",
        Failing => " (failing)",
        _ => " (waiting)"
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// The head commit's checks, failures first, then the ones still running, then
    /// the ones that passed — in GitHub's order within each — up to
    /// <see cref="ChecksShown"/>, and the rest counted. Counted against GitHub's own
    /// total as well as the list, because the list stops at the client's limit and
    /// the counts do not.
    /// </summary>
    private static RenderFragment ChecksList(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull) => __builder =>
    {
        var ordered = pull.HeadChecks.OrderBy(check => CheckRank(check.State)).ToList();
        var shown = ordered.Take(ChecksShown).ToList();
        var total = Math.Max(pull.CheckCounts?.Total ?? 0, pull.HeadChecks.Count);
        var hidden = total - shown.Count;

        <ul class="pull-request-detail-checks" data-testid="pull-request-detail-checks">
            @if (total == 0)
            {
                <li class="pull-request-detail-checks__more">No checks have reported yet.</li>
            }
            @foreach (var check in shown)
            {
                var state = CheckSlug(check.State);
                <li class="@($"pull-request-detail-checks__check pull-request-detail-checks__check--{state}")" data-check-state="@state">
                    <span class="pull-request-detail-checks__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(check.Url))
                    {
                        <a class="pull-request-detail-checks__name" href="@check.Url" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@check.Name</a>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <span class="pull-request-detail-checks__name">@check.Name</span>
                    }
                    <span class="pull-request-detail-checks__word">@CheckWord(check)</span>
                </li>
            }
            @if (shown.Count == 0 && total > 0)
            {
                <li class="pull-request-detail-checks__more">@($"{total} checks, not listed one by one.")</li>
            }
            else if (hidden > 0)
            {
                <li class="pull-request-detail-checks__more">@(HiddenAllPassed(pull, shown) ? $"and {hidden} more passed" : $"and {hidden} more")</li>
            }
        </ul>
    };

    private static int CheckRank(GitHubCheckState state) => state switch
    {
        GitHubCheckState.Failing => 0,
        GitHubCheckState.Pending => 1,
        GitHubCheckState.Passing or GitHubCheckState.None => 2
    };

    private static string CheckSlug(GitHubCheckState state) => state switch
    {
        GitHubCheckState.Failing => "failed",
        GitHubCheckState.Pending => "running",
        GitHubCheckState.Passing or GitHubCheckState.None => "passed"
    };

    /// <summary>Failed, Running, or how long a passed one took — "2m 10s", "45s".</summary>
    private static string CheckWord(GitHubCheck check) => check.State switch
    {
        GitHubCheckState.Failing => "Failed",
        GitHubCheckState.Pending => "Running",
        GitHubCheckState.Passing or GitHubCheckState.None => check.Duration is { } duration ? DurationWords(duration) : "Passed"
    };

    private static string DurationWords(TimeSpan duration) =>
        duration >= TimeSpan.FromMinutes(1)
            ? $"{(int)duration.TotalMinutes}m {duration.Seconds}s"
            : $"{Math.Max(0, (int)duration.TotalSeconds)}s";

    /// <summary>Whether every check the list leaves out passed: none of the listed
    /// ones past the cut failed or is running, and GitHub's counts have no failure or
    /// running check the listed ones do not already account for.</summary>
    private static bool HiddenAllPassed(GitHubOpenPullRequest pull, IReadOnlyList<GitHubCheck> shown)
    {
        var shownUnfinished = shown.Count(check => check.State is GitHubCheckState.Failing or GitHubCheckState.Pending);
        var listedUnfinished = pull.HeadChecks.Count(check => check.State is GitHubCheckState.Failing or GitHubCheckState.Pending);
        var countedUnfinished = pull.CheckCounts is { } counts ? counts.Failed + counts.Pending : listedUnfinished;

        return Math.Max(listedUnfinished, countedUnfinished) == shownUnfinished;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The pin, in the detail's head of both views where the host composed a pins
    /// store. A toggle whose name stays "Pin #n" while <c>aria-pressed</c> carries
    /// whether it is pinned — the button pattern's way, so a screen reader says the
    /// state once rather than in the name and the state both. The visible word is the
    /// name's, so a reader who speaks the label reaches it.
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment PinToggle(string repositoryFullName, int number) => __builder =>
    {
        if (_pins is null) return;

        var pinned = IsPinned(repositoryFullName, number);
        <ToggleButton Pressed="@pinned"
                      PressedChanged="_ => TogglePin(repositoryFullName, number)"
                      AriaLabel="@($"Pin #{number}")"
                      Title="@(pinned ? "Pinned: listed whatever the filters say, until you unpin it." : "Pin: keep it listed whatever the filters say, and after it merges or closes.")"
                      CssClass="btn--small pull-request-detail__pin"
                      TestId="pull-request-pin">
            Pin
        </ToggleButton>
    };

    /// <summary>The task the pull request is related to, among every task — not only
    /// mine, so Everyone's rows lead back to their task too.</summary>
    private DeliveryRunReference? TaskFor(BoardRow row) =>
        PullRequestTask?.Invoke(row.Open is { } open ? TaskSubject(open) : TaskSubject(row.MergedPull!), false);

    private static IntegrationLinkRef TaskLink(DeliveryRunReference task) =>
        new(task.EntryId?.ToString() ?? task.Label, IntegrationProvider.None, IntegrationLinkKind.Other, task.Label, Title: $"Open {task.Label} in the task list");

    private EventCallback<IntegrationLinkRef> TaskOpener(DeliveryRunReference task) =>
        OnOpenTask.HasDelegate
            ? EventCallback.Factory.Create<IntegrationLinkRef>(this, () => OnOpenTask.InvokeAsync(task))
            : default;

    /// <summary>
    /// The session behind a pull request: the one whose transcript recorded its
    /// address, else the most recently active one on its head branch in its
    /// repository. The second is a match on two facts the agent and GitHub both
    /// state, not a guess — but a branch name can be reused, so the address wins
    /// whenever there is one.
    /// </summary>
    internal AgentSession? SessionFor(string url, string headRefName, string repositoryFullName)
    {
        var recorded = _sessions
            .Where(session => session.PullRequests?.Any(link =>
                string.Equals(link.Url, url, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)) == true)
            .MaxBy(session => session.LastActivityAt);

        if (recorded is not null) return recorded;

        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(headRefName)) return null;

        return _sessions
            .Where(session => string.Equals(session.Branch, headRefName, StringComparison.Ordinal)
                && (SameRepository(session.Repository, repositoryFullName)
                    || SameRepository(session.ResolvedRepository, repositoryFullName)))
            .MaxBy(session => session.LastActivityAt);
    }

    /// <summary>Whether a session's repository — recorded as <c>owner/name</c> or,
    /// on a replicated record, as an alias — is the pull request's.</summary>
    private bool SameRepository(string? sessionRepository, string fullName) =>
        !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(sessionRepository)
        && (string.Equals(sessionRepository, fullName, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
            || (AliasOf(sessionRepository) is { } alias
                && string.Equals(alias, AliasOf(fullName), StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)));

    private static IntegrationLinkRef SessionLink(AgentSession session) =>
        IntegrationLinkRef.Session(
            session.Id,
            SessionLabel(session),
            session.Kind is AgentSessionKind.Copilot ? IntegrationProvider.Copilot : IntegrationProvider.Claude,
            session.State switch
            {
                AgentSessionState.Running => IntegrationSessionState.Running,
                AgentSessionState.Stalled => IntegrationSessionState.Stalled,
                _ => IntegrationSessionState.Finished
            },
            title: $"Session {session.Id} — open in Sessions");

    /// <summary>The session's title, or the first eight characters of its id where it
    /// has none of its own — a replicated record names itself with its id.</summary>
    private static string SessionLabel(AgentSession session) =>
        !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(session.Title) && !string.Equals(session.Title, session.Id, StringComparison.Ordinal)
            ? session.Title
            : session.Id.Length <= 8 ? session.Id : session.Id[..8];

    private EventCallback<IntegrationLinkRef> SessionOpener =>
        OnOpenSession.HasDelegate
            ? EventCallback.Factory.Create<IntegrationLinkRef>(this, (IntegrationLinkRef link) => OnOpenSession.InvokeAsync(link.Id))
            : default;
}
